# ROE ticket flow

Agents follow this sequence for every new ROE ticket **without the user restating it**. Skip a step only if the user explicitly says so (e.g. “docs-only” or “hotfix”).

## Naming (required)

| Surface | Format |
|---------|--------|
| Issue / PR | `[ROE-NNN] Short title (ABC-NNN)` — omit `(ABC-NNN)` if no workstream alias |
| Commit | `[ROE-NNN][ABC-NNN] imperative message` — or `[ROE-NNN] message` if no alias |
| Branch | `feature/ROE-NNN-kebab-slug` from fresh `origin/develop` |

**ROE-NNN** is the global serial (never skip). Next free is tracked in `project.md` / `.lovable/plan.md`.

## Sequence

1. **Audit** — Read CONTEXT_PLAN (+ CURSOR.md if touching `src/` or `supabase/`). Search before inventing. Prefer a canvas for multi-finding audits.
2. **Impact analysis** — Write `docs/ROE-NNN-*-impact-analysis.md` (problem, acceptance, scope, files, test plan, **deploy/ops**). Await user approval before coding unless they already said “implement”.
3. **Branch** — `git fetch origin develop && git checkout -b feature/ROE-NNN-… origin/develop`
4. **Implement** — Minimal diff; honor sync pairs; add/adjust Vitest for scoring/dietary/intent/pairings.
5. **Ask EXAMPLES chips (when applicable)** — If the ticket adds or changes **user-discoverable Ask capability** (new intent enums, situational modes, dietary/wellness/lens paths, cuisine modes, etc.), either update `src/pages/Ask.tsx` `EXAMPLES` in the same PR **or** queue an explicit follow-up ROE in TODO/plan — do not silently ship engine-only discovery gaps. *(This is UI “Or try” chips — not GitHub Labels.)*
6. **Docs sync** — Same PR: `TODO.md`, `.lovable/plan.md`, `.cursor/CONTEXT_PLAN.md`, relevant CURSOR.md, next-free ROE bump.
7. **Ship** — Commit → push → `gh pr create` (title matches issue) → ensure a tracking **Issue** exists with the same title → add Issue + PR to Rasaoi QA Board → set Status **In progress**.
8. **GitHub Labels (required on Issue + PR)** — Never leave Labels empty on board items. Apply the repo taxonomy (see `.github/PROJECT_BOARD.md`):
   - **type:** `type:feature` | `type:bug` | `type:qa` (add `type:qa` when Status moves to QA / needs stakeholder Pass)
   - **priority:** exactly one of `priority:P0` | `priority:P1` | `priority:P2` | `priority:P3` (drives board Priority via `project-board.yml`)
   - **area:** one or more of `area:ask` | `area:reading` | `area:lab` | `area:catalog`
   - Optional: `blocked`, `needs-repro`
   ```bash
   gh issue edit <n> --add-label "type:feature,priority:P2,area:ask"
   gh pr edit <n> --add-label "type:feature,priority:P2,area:ask"
   ```
9. **Ops / deploy** — In the PR body, state exactly what is required after merge:
   - Frontend: Vercel auto-deploy on `develop` / `main` (note if none).
   - Edge: `npx supabase functions deploy <name> --no-verify-jwt` for each touched function (often `parse-intent`).
   - DB: `npm run supabase:db:push` when migrations land; regenerate types if schema changed.
   - Culinary index: `node scripts/personal/build-culinary-index.mjs` when matrix/registry sources change.
10. **QA closeout** — After merge: run noted ops; ensure Issue+PR have `type:qa`; board Status → **QA**; stakeholder Pass → **Done**.

## Do not

- Commit secrets or `supabase/.temp/*`
- Skip impact analysis for non-trivial product changes
- Invent APIs/tables not in CONTEXT_PLAN without searching first
- Use `IP-FIX` / `FUL` / `ASK` as the sole ID — always assign **ROE-NNN** and append alias
- Ship new Ask-parse capability without either Ask EXAMPLES updates or a queued follow-up ROE
- Leave Issue/PR **Labels** empty on the Rasaoi QA Board (Priority on the board will stay blank without `priority:P*`)
